       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A family visit and the timing of evening rounds don't change the risk. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the labeled maximum, and it could cause GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, or cardiovascular harm. You've told me the dose is intentional, but you haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding the limit. I can't enter a dose with this much potential for harm on that basis.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose.\n- **Enter a lower dose or interval,** such as 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours, if the goal is analgesia.\n- **Add a GI-protection order,** such as a PPI, alongside either of those.\n\nIf you think the patient needs more than the standard maximum, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy or a clinical pharmacologist first. You could also enter the order directly through your institution's override process, which has pharmacist verification. I can still help with other orders for this patient."
